From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] secur32: schannel's QueryCredentialsAttributesW(SECPKG_CRED_ATTR_NAMES) answers as the A one.

Credentials without a certificate have no names: SEC_E_NO_CREDENTIALS, which the A function already
gives and Windows gives (secur32 schannel tests). The W function said SEC_E_UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTION.
---
diff --git a/dlls/secur32/schannel.c b/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
index 997ba17..15ee114 100644
--- a/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
+++ b/dlls/secur32/schannel.c
@@ -372,9 +372,15 @@ static SECURITY_STATUS SEC_ENTRY schan_QueryCredentialsAttributesW(
     switch (ulAttribute)
     {
     case SECPKG_CRED_ATTR_NAMES:
-        FIXME("SECPKG_CRED_ATTR_NAMES: stub\n");
+        /* Stained Glass OS: as the A function, which Windows answers so for credentials without a
+         * certificate (secur32 schannel tests); was SEC_E_UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTION */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_SCH_NAMES_W
         ret = SEC_E_UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTION;
         break;
+#endif
+        FIXME("SECPKG_CRED_ATTR_NAMES: stub\n");
+        ret = SEC_E_NO_CREDENTIALS;
+        break;
     default:
         ret = schan_QueryCredentialsAttributes(phCredential, ulAttribute,
          pBuffer);
